    # Convert fixed-width table to tab separated, preserving header conversion.
    # Canned machinable versions exist for all-versions; for per-lang we can convert by splitting columns based on header positions? Simpler: use dynamic generation from parsed tables where possible (fields/kinds-full etc). For other lists (features etc) canned mach exists for global.
    lines=txt.splitlines()
    out=[]
